  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirement\nFind the software requirements for iPhones that support AirDrop's ability to continue transmitting over the web (internet) when out of range.\n\n## Screenshot Evidence\n\n**Screenshot 1:** Shows a Google search initiated with the query \"AirDrop continue transfer over internet when out of range iPhone software requirements\" — directly aligned with the task.\n\n**Screenshot 2:** The Google search results page contains an AI Overview that explicitly states: *\"Continuing an AirDrop transfer over the internet or cellular data when moving out of range requires **iOS 17.1 or later** on your iPhone.\"* It further lists \"Operating System: iOS 17.1 or later installed on both iPhones\" under Software & System Requirements. Additionally, the Apple Support result snippet confirms: *\"If you leave Bluetooth or Wi-Fi range after an AirDrop transfer is initiated, the transfer continues over the internet.\"*\n\n**Screenshots 3–5:** The Apple iPhone User Guide page (\"Use AirDrop on iPhone to send items to nearby Apple devices\") confirms the feature description with the note: *\"If you leave Bluetooth or Wi-Fi range after an AirDrop transfer is initiated, the transfer continues over the internet.\"* The page also shows a \"Turn off cellular data for AirDrop\" section, corroborating the internet/cellular fallback feature.\n\n## Response Consistency\nThe response states the requirement is **iOS 17.1 or later**, which directly matches the AI Overview content visible in Screenshot 2. The cited Apple User Guide quote in the response matches the text shown in Screenshots 3–5. This is also factually accurate — the AirDrop-over-internet feature was introduced in iOS 17.1.\n\n## Conclusion\nThe task asked for the software requirement, and both the browsing process (search → Apple documentation) and the final answer correctly identify **iOS 17.1 or later** as the requirement, supported by visible screenshot evidence.\n\n**Verdict: SUCCESS**",
